    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you just said it's a \"significant hurdle\" and that many arguments are \"legally tenuous\". isnt that basically saying the old way of looking at it is dead? if the court has basically decided the amendment protects an individual right to carry, aren't the people pushing for strict bans just arguing against the law at this point?",
