    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The ruling established a baseline right, but it did not create an absolute, unfettered license to carry any weapon without restriction. Proponents of strict control are not arguing against the law; they are arguing that the current interpretation of the Second Amendment is too broad and must be narrowly construed to allow for reasonable public safety regulations. The debate is now about defining the *scope* of the right, not whether the right exists at all.",
      "source": "target",
